#: includes/tab-instructions.php:19 includes/tabs-output.php:31
msgid "Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:21
msgid "This plugin lets you create events - holidays, webinars, achievements, notable historical figures, or anything else with a start (and optional end) date - and display upcoming ones in a widget or via a shortcode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:24
msgid "Add a new Event from the Events menu, and give it a title, an outline (shown as the excerpt), and optionally a body and featured image."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:25
msgid "Fill in its Event Details in the sidebar metabox - a start date and time are required; only set an end date if the event runs across more than one day. Location is a free-text field and is optional."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:26
msgid "Optionally assign one or more Categories to the event, so it can be filtered in the widget or shortcode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:27
msgid "Publish the event. It will stop appearing in the widget/shortcode output once its end date (or start date, for a one-day event) has passed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:30 includes/tab-widget.php:24 includes/tabs-output.php:28
msgid "Widget"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:31
msgid "Add the Events widget to a sidebar from Appearance > Widgets. Its default title, category, image size, and date format can be set on the Widget tab, and overridden per-widget-instance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:33
msgid "Shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:35
msgid "Display a single event by its slug: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:38
msgid "Display multiple upcoming events, optionally filtered by category: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:41 includes/tabs-output.php:30
msgid "To X Integration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:46
msgid "If %s is installed and active, enable integration on the To X Integration tab to automatically post (and optionally repost) an event a set number of days before it starts. Per-event timing and post text/media can be overridden from the Autopost to X and Post to X boxes shown on each event once integration is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:52
msgid "Timezones"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tab-instructions.php:53
msgid "All \"is this event over yet\" checks and scheduled post/repost times use your site\\'s configured timezone (Settings > General > Timezone), not the timezone of the server itself."
msgstr ""

